 Bahniuk (she/her) is a Ukrainian-Canadian theatre designer originally from Edmonton and now resides in Brooklyn, New York. She is a graduate of the Masters of Fine Arts in Design program at the Yale School of Drama and a recipient of the Jay Keene and Jean Griffin Keene Prize in Costume Design. Recent credits include production design for Alina, Barvinok and Michael Mysterious (Pyretic Productions), costume and scenic design for Subscribe or Like (Workshop West), costume design for Pride and Prejudice (Yale Dramatic Association) and A Midsummer Night's Dream (Classical Theatre of Harlem) and scenic design for Yaga (Belfry Theatre). Stephanie was also the Costume Department Coordinator for And Just Like That Season 2, the Sex and the City reboot with HBO Max. She has multiple Elizabeth Sterling Haynes nominations for her work and received the award for Outstanding Set Design in 2017 for Stupid Fucking Bird (Edmonton Actors Theatre). Stephanie is also union member of Local 829 and an Artistic Associate of Pyretic Productions. \nStephanie is available for work across the country and holds an O-1 visa for work in the United States. \nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
