 in theatre and live performance. Their work spans composition, sound design, and technical direction, with a focus on creating immersive sonic environments. Their recent roles include Audio Engineer and Technical Coordinator for the Small World Music Festival and Global Toronto, Stages Coordinator for Sunfest, and Technical Director/Stage Manager for Corpus Dance Projects' internationally touring show La Bulle. Their design work was featured in the Canadian National Exhibition at the prestigious 2023 Prague Quadrennial.\nCredits:\n2026\nSound Designer- Murder on the Orient Express- Theatre Northwest\nSound Designer- Silence- Douglas College\n2025\nSound Designer- Carry the one - Tara Cheyenne Performance\nCo-Sound Designer- Right Thing to Be Doing- SFU\n2024\nSound Designer- Hound of Baskervilles- Theatre Northwest\nSound Designer- Further Than The Furthest Thing- Douglas College\n2023\nTouring AV Technician/ Show Operator- La Bulle - Corpus Dance Projects\nFeatured Artist - Prague Quadrennial Exhibition of Countries and Regions\nAssistant Lighting Designer- Vierge- Factory Theatre\nAssistant Sound Designer- Redbone Coonhound- Tarragon Theatre\n2022\nSound Engineer- Apocalypse Play- Common Boots Theatre\nLighting Designer- Sleeping, Tucked in a Lonely Purple- Tiger Princess Dance Projects\nTrailer Sound Designer- 10th Anniversary Podcast Series- Red Beti Theatre\nSound Designer- Designing The Revolution- Associated Designers of Canada\n2021\nAssistant Lighting Designer- A Tonic For Desperate Times- Theatre Gargantua\nLighting Designer- Take me to your garden- Hamilton Fringe Festival\nAssistant Sound Designer- You Can’t get there from here- Factory Theatre\n \nProfile Photo by Sara Naimpour (https://www.saranaimpour.com)\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .