, Latvian, RussianResidence — RegionMontrealFacebookFacebookInstagramInstagramBioMeghan Moe Beitiks (she/they) works with associations and disassociations of culture/nature/structure. They were a Fulbright Student Fellow in Scenography to Latvia and a recipient of the Edes Foundation Prize for Emerging Artists. They have designed lights for the California Academy of Sciences, the Asian Art Museum, SF Sketchfest, Atom-R, David Herrera Performance Company, and Yoshi's Jazz Club. They've also designed media and sets for Concerts Under the Stars at the Chaffee Planetarium at the Grand Rapids Public Museum. They received their BA in Theater Arts from the University of California at Santa Cruz, and their MFA in Performance Art from the School of the Art Institute of Chicago.  \nThey analyze perceptions of ecology though the lenses of site, history, emotions, and their own body in order to produce work that examines relationships with the non-human. The work emerges as video, performance, installation, writing or photography depending on what arises from her process of research and improvisation, and have worked in many kinds of collaborative processes. \nThey have presented work in California, Chicago, Brooklyn, Wales, London, Latvia, Australia and Russia. They have been a MacDowell Colony Fellow, an OxBow LeRoy Neiman Fellow, and a Bemis Artist in Residence. They are currently an Assistant Professor in the Department of Theatre at Concordia University, with a focus on Ecology, Performance and Design.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\