n. He received his BFA Honours in Theatre Design at the University of Saskatchewan under the training and mentorship of Ken MacKenzie and Carla Orosz. Cody’s practice is majorly focused on sustainability in theatre and ecoscenography, and he is passionate about utilizing new sustainable materials, design for deconstruction, and reducing the environmental impacts of theatre. Cody will be attending the MFA Theatre Design program at the University of Alberta beginning in the Fall of 2025.\nSelect credits include Lighting Design for Souffler la veilleuse (La Troupe du Jour, 2025), The Music Man (Saskatoon Summer Players, 2024) Metamorphosis (Greystone Theatre, 2024), Sound Design for 10 out of 12 (Greystone Theatre, 2024), Set Design for Rooftops (Wonder City Collective, 2025), Mary of Patuanak and Leave it to Weavers (Gordon Tootoosis Nīkānīwin Theatre, 2023 & 2024),The Mirror of Venus and Paris, Without Return (University of Alberta’s New Works Festival, 2020) and The Insanity of Mary Girard (Mad Hatter Theatre Company, 2018).\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
