ition of Manager, Theatre Operations at the Arts Umbrella, a non-profit in Vancouver that provides arts education in the fields of Theatre, Music & Film, Dance and Art & Design. As a Set and Lighting Designer Brodie worked in Canadian theatre, dance and opera from 1989. He designed for English language theatres across Canada, major summer festivals and ballet companies at home and abroad. Brodie was recognized with Jessie, Dora, Betty Mitchell and Sterling Awards, as well as a Bay Area Theatre Critics Circle Award. He has taught at UBC, the National Theatre School, the Banff Centre and Studio 58 / Langara College. Brodie has a BFA in design from UBC and an MFA in directing from UVic. He lives in Vancouver.\nAvailable for Work?NoAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkNo\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
