ume designer from Cornwall, Ontario, currently residing in Toronto. She is a recent graduate of York University's Theatre Production and Design program. Millie has been recognized for her design work and potential as an emerging artist, having won the \"Best Set Design\" award at the 2024 and 2026 York University playGround Festivals and the Temple Harris Book Prize 2026, awarded to an outstanding fine arts student at York University. She was the set and props designer for Gringas (First Born Theatre Co.), which was included in the Toronto Star's \"Top 10 Theatre Productions of 2024\", and received glowing reviews from critics.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
