 MacPherson Playhouse, Vancouver Playhouse, Pacific Theatre, Edmonton's Citadel Theatre (designed 35 productions), Phoenix Theatre, and Northern Light Theatre, Alberta Theatre Projects, Theatre Calgary, Saskatoon's 25th Street Theatre, Regina's Globe Theatre, Toronto’s Canadian Stage and Royal Alexandra, and Ottawa's National Arts Centre. He served as Resident Designer at Edmonton’s Citadel Theatre and the Phoenix Theatre in the 1980s. He has received a Dora Award in Toronto, and two Sterling Awards in Edmonton for his designs. He has also designed in the USA, Ghana, Scotland, and Egypt. Stancil taught for 42 years in Canada, the USA, Ghana, and Egypt before retiring in 2016. He is currently Professor Emeritus at the American University in Cairo.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkNo\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
