. CHOI (she/her) composes music for film and TV [recently: Last of the Right Whales, Apocalypse Plan B (CBC); Relax I’m From the Future (Universal)] and designs sonic environments for live performance [recently: A Wrinkle in Time (Stratford Festival), The Darkest Dark (Young People’s Theatre), Things I Know to Be True (Company Theatre/Mirvish)]. She has served in artist residencies at the Canadian Film Centre Slaight Music Lab, Banff Centre, and SOCAN Foundation. She is an award-winning violinist, educator, and formerly studied behavioural neuroscience. She is the 2020 laureate of the Pauline McGibbon Award, and nominated for the Louis Applebaum Award, 2 Robert Merritt Awards, and a Canadian Screen Music Award. Deanna is a member of IATSE ADC 659 and the Screen Composers’ Guild. She lives in T’karonto on Treaty 13 Territory.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkNo\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
