m a multidisciplinary artist with a focus in video/projection design for live performance. My work is now based in Tkaronto/Toronto, but I began my career in K'jipuktuk/Halifax, NS, where I completed technical theatre and stage design studies at the Fountain School of Performing Arts. \nI believe there is a magic to visual media in helping us express thoughtful and intimate stories - especially when the creation process is supported by mindfulness and compassion.\nFor the past 5 years, I have grown my creative interest in mixed-media/collage design, cohesive aesthetics, and video design as more than just a place-making tool. Whether it’s opera, dance, music, or theatre, my creative process thrives on early and intimate collaboration with directors and designers. I then take delight in \"building from scratch\", using my skills in video/photo manipulation, hand-drawn animation and illustration, and growing skills in 3D animation. \nOutside of video design, I have experience in film sound, lighting, scenic painting, and I find so much joy in my own creative pursuits in digital/fine art, crafting, and music-making.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
