nAydin Dezell (They/Them) is a multi-disciplinary theatre artist from Brantford, Ontario, working primarily as a lighting designer for theatre and live performance. Their practice centres on narrative-driven lighting design, with a focus on shaping atmosphere, rhythm, and audience attention in performance environments.\nBeyond theatre, Aydin has worked across the live events industry on stages both large and small, collaborating with artists across a wide range of acts and genres. Their work is grounded in a curiosity for how technical systems and creative intent intersect, and how design decisions influence perception and experience in real time.\nAydin studied Technical Production for the Performing Arts Industry at Sheridan College before continuing their training at the National Theatre School of Canada in the Production Design and Technical Arts program, where they remain now (Class of 2027).\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
