n designer. Select company credits include, Alberta Theatre Projects, The Arts Club Theatre Company, Bard on The Beach, Calgary Opera, Citadel Theatre, Pacific Opera Victoria, Ruby Slippers, Saint John Theatre Company, Shaw Festival, Studio 58, Théâtre la Seizième. In 2019-2020 season Corwin worked as Head of Projection Technology at the Banff Centre for Arts and Creativity. \nFor his designs Corwin has earned a Robert Merritt Award, the CITT/ICTS Technical Merit Award, and has been nominated for three Jessie Richardson Awards, three Betty Mitchell Awards and an Elizabeth Sterling Award.\nCorwin has studied animation, was a co-founder of Awkward Stage Productions and Flip The Switch Collective, has worked as a storyteller with Forbidden Vancouver Historic Walking Tours, as well as an urban game designer/operator with Vancouver Mysteries.\nIn theatre, Corwin’s professional experience includes: acting, directing, video/projection design, graphic design, set and props design, technical direction. Corwin is a Studio 58 acting graduate and holds a Bachelor’s degree in Performing Arts from Capilano University.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
