n for art, design, and performance.  She received her BFA in Theatre from York University's Performance Creation and Design program, during her time at York she worked as a Set Designer for the Devised Theatre Festival.  Since graduating she has garnered credits in both theatre and film; currently working as the Set, Costume & Props Designer for Bird On Stage's new production The Twin Sues by Garrett M. Ryan. She recently worked under Gillian Gallow's mentorship as the Design Assistant for the Canadian Stage production of A Doll’s House. She was also the Assistant Set Designer for The Sankofa Trilogy by Watah Theatre at the Theatre Centre and was the Set, Costume & Props Designer for the Toronto Fringe show Koli Kari by Ganesh Thava.  Other credits include Set Design for the short film Cherry On Top, Production Assistant for Shadowland Theatre, Costume and Props Assistant for TFO, Scenic Painting for Coal Mine Theatre.  Outside of theatre and film, Madeleine works as the Uniform Lead at the Canadian Opera Company.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
