 the traditional unceded territory of the Algonquin Anishinabeg. \nHe has completed my MFA in Theatre Design at the University of Alberta, which is a program that focuses on scenery, costume, and lighting. \nHis has previously worked with the Citadel Theatre, Globe Theatre, Theatre Network, University of Alberta, MacEwan University, a Company of Fools, Shadow Theatre, Amoris Projects, Azimuth Theatre, Tiny Bear Jaws, Alberta Musical Theatre Company, So. Glad Arts, fenceless theatre, Silver Skate Festival, Good Women Dance Collective, and Mile Zero Dance. He has designed sets for various cross-country touring productions, theatre festivals, and unconventional performance spaces. A bulk of his theatrical resume lies in the development and realization of new work.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
