ence — Province/TerritoryAlbertaLanguages SpokenEnglishBioBeyata is a queer, half-Chinese set & costume designer currently living with a beloved gaggle of friends and dogs in Edmonton. Her theatrical origins stem from a partially-traumatic childhood in musical theatre and a love of illustration. Her favourite pieces to collaborate on are newly-developed works, re-contextualized canonical shows, and movement-based/musically-driven theatre. She has an especial love of shows that embrace non-reality and the absurd. Also, she has an embarrassingly soft spot for Sondheim.\nBeyata is a graduate of the UofA's Theatre Design program and splits her time between Edmonton and out-of-province contracts (but is trying to stay closer to home so she can spend more time cuddling dogs). She's worked as an assistant designer at the Shaw Festival for the past 3 seasons, having been a part of 14 shows over the years and has just recently started designing her own shows there. She's also assisted at the Citadel, Banff, Freewill, and will be associating at the Winter Garden in Toronto this December. She can sort-of juggle for 30-second stints on a good day.\nSelected Credits: The Secret Garden, Village Wooing, Playboy of the Western World, Overruled, Bright Lights (Shaw Festival); Little Shop of Horrors (Artsclub/Citadel co-pro); Jersey Boys (Citadel); Metronome, MOB (Workshop West); Freaky Green Eyes (Screaming Mantis Productions); Sleight of Mind (WCT), EDAY (Theatre Network); Julius Caesar, A Midsummer Night's Dream (Malachites); Silence, Bug, Eurydice, All Fall Down, Medea (UofA Studio Theatre)\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\t