atford, Ontario, specializing in creating designs that elevate and reflect the story. She has designed for theatres across Ontario, crafting dynamic, audience‑engaging sets with practical mechanics and visually compelling costumes. Her costume design for ERASED (2024) earned a nomination for Outstanding Costume Design (General Theatre Division) at the 45th Dora Mavor Moore Awards. Known for her collaborative approach, Jung A works closely with directors and production teams, seamlessly blending creativity and technical precision to bring stories vividly to life on stage.\n \nCredits :\nSet  - Beyonsea and the Mothers, Late Company (Green-Light Arts production), Shakespeare's N***a (The Langham Director's Workshop at Stratford Festival), Indecent(National Theatre School of Canada) / Set and Costume - Harabogee(할아버지) and Me (Shakespeare in Action) / Costume - Erased(Open Heart Surgery Theatre & Theatre Passe-Muraile), Macbeth, The Fall of the House of Atreus(The Langham Director's Workshop at Stratford Festival), I got my life back! (National Theatre School of Canada)\n \nWebsite: http://www.imjunga.com\n \n \nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkNo\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
