dence — RegionStratfordInstagramInstagramLinkedInLinkedInBioKaileigh Krysztofiak is a lighting designer, arts manager, and creative leader with a growing international presence in public art and performance. As the founding General Manager of Lights On Stratford, Kaileigh has helped establish the festival as a destination for immersive art. They also manage North American partnerships for Sydney-based studio Amigo & Amigo, supporting cross-border collaborations in public and experiential design.\nKaileigh teaches at the National Theatre School of Canada and is a member of ADC and IATSE Local 659. Their work spans theatre, festivals, and large-scale installations, with collaborations including Stratford Festival, Mirvish, Soulpepper, and others. Kaileigh has been recognized with two Dora Award nominations and Pauline McGibbon Award nominations in 2020 and 2023.\nDriven by a love of storytelling and community connection, Kaileigh continues to shape cultural experiences across North America and beyond.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkNo\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
