        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\tChange your cover photoUpload Change your cover photoUpload\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tApply\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t Cancel\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\tAshley Naomi Skye\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tThis user account status is Approved\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAbout\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAbout\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPosts\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPosts\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tComments\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tComments\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\tThis user has not added any information to their profile yet.Member TypeAssociate MemberE-mail Addressnaomiskye33@icloud.comRepresentative and Contact Self-represented\nEmail: naomiskye33@icloud.com\nWebsite URLhttps://ashleynaomi.squarespace.com/Phone Number289-400-6958Design Discipline(s)SoundPreferred Pronoun(s)she/herResidence — Province/TerritoryOntarioLanguages SpokenEnglishResidence — RegionToronto, MontrealInstagramInstagramLinkedInLinkedInBioAshley Naomi Skye (she/her), is a trans femme theatre artist, actor/performer, and musician/sound designer. Excited by fusing lines between emotions, genres, and mediatic forms, Ashley’s creative process uses a post-modern, kaleidoscopic approach influenced by remix culture, blending digital+embodied motifs to evoke colourful feelings of synesthesia.\nAshley is the 2026 laureate of the Ontario Arts Council’s Pauline McGibbon Award, and a winner of the Toronto Theatre Critics’ Award for Best Original Sound Design for The Veil.\nCurrently, she is developing the original plays digitrans // analogirl and Hip Hop 100, which were respectively presented as in-development staged readings via Dead Name Theatre and Tarragon Theatre’s Greenhouse Festival in 2024. The former play has been supported by SummerWorks 2025 and Community One’s Rainbow Grant, and was foreshadowed by an interactive rhythm-game style performance at Buddies in Bad Times’ 2024 Rhubarb Festival.\nIn 2025, Ashley has been re-establishing herself as an actor through training with Theatre Gym, Theatre Potluck, and Shakespeare Bash’d; having performed in Museum of Toronto’s The 52 Live at Luminato Festival, and ACTRA Toronto’s “Working the Scene in Colour” for Thembani Mdluli’s in-development screenplay Where the Rivers Meet.\nAshley begins 2026 as part of Black Theatre Workshop’s AMP program with mentor Keshia Palm, further expansion into Montreal via Centaur Theatre’s WinterWorks Festival (sound design for Marie Barlizo’s The Healing), and her Stratford debut with a Halloween remount of The Veil at Meighen Forum. Her sound designs continue to travel across Canada with touring remounts of Regarding Antigone (Vancouver’s rEvolver Festival, 2026) and The Veil (Calgary’s Vertigo Theatre, 2027).\nAshley is driven by contemporary and adapted work that reflects freshness, energy, emotional truth, blurred binaries, and deep introspection - she beats to the ebbing-and-flowing rhythms of the cycle of life, both raw and tender, in the name of healing and taking care from our grief. Ashley is interested not simply in what is being told and being seen, but in counternarratives to mainstream hegemony.\nAs a live bassist+keyboardist+MC, Ashley has performed with Confluence Concerts (Side by Side, 2024), Femmepocalypse (2023), Exit Points (editions #59 and #68, 2025-2026). She has released the instrumental albums Synesthesia and Moonlight Museum independently via Bandcamp. She will next be organizing the ambient concert series Wave Pool with collaborators Sonia Leung and Yamen Mouhanna in Toronto.\n \nSelect recent credits: The Healing (Centaur Theatre: WinterWorks), The Veil (Thought for Food, Guild Festival Theatre, and Crow's Theatre), Gringas (First Born Theatre), The Drowsy Chaperone (Shifting Ground Collective), The Little Prince (Theatre Passe Muraille), Orbit (Waxwing Theatre), Isle of Demons & The 39 Steps (Guild Festival Theatre), Tiger Lilies (Aluna Theatre: Caminos Festival).\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
