ustainability and ecosystems, JB hopes to grow and cultivate a practice that supports their fellow collaborators, the stories they wish to tell, and the places where we get to tell them. They have been fortunate to work across Canada from Ontario to Newfoundland, most notably with the Stephenville Theatre Festival (2024) and Neptune Theatre (2026). JB has held teaching appointments at York University where they supervised the Scenic Art and Prop Making Practicum Students (2023-2024), and speaking engagements at Queen’s University. \nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
