CloudSoundCloudBioRiver is a queer, Mad, & disabled multidisciplinary artist in Toronto, Ontario. The themes they are most interested in exploring in their work are those of queerness, grief, survival, and community. As a designer & musician who works in multiple mediums, he is interested in the ways that different art forms can come together to create living, breathing things we call stories. One of their favourite parts of the artistic process is collaborating with others to explore new ideas, and new ways to collectively make work that is experimental, fulfilling, and joyful. Their work often plays with elements of heightened reality, poetic lyricism, and queer re-imaginings of folk & fairy tales.\nAs a Sound Designer they have been a part of Paprika Festival's Design Lab under the mentorship of Mickey Rodriguez & Steph Raposo. They have most recently been Sound Designer for 11:11 at Theatre Passe Muraille & Prairie Theatre Exchange (2021), as well as rihannaboi95 at Young People's Theatre (2021).\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
