s SpokenEnglishFacebookFacebookInstagramInstagramBioWes Pearce (he/him/his) continues to be privileged to have been raised, to play and now to work in and around the traditional lands of the Treaty 4 peoples; the nêhiyawak, Anihšināpēk, Dakota, Lakota, and Nakoda, and the homeland of the Métis/Michif Nation. These contested lands are the lands of ever-changing skies, of cold winters and hot summers and a landscape of dynamic wonder that continues to astonish, inform and inspire.\nHe is currently Professor in the Theatre Department at the University of Regina where he teaches classes in costume and set design, Canadian Theatre and pop culture. He served as the department/governance/curricular lead on a brand new BFA in devised performance and theatre creation which launched in September 2022.\n He has designed elements for over 100 productions including numerous credits for the University of Regina, the Globe Theatre (Regina), Persephone Theatre (Saskatoon), Stage West Calgary as well as PTE (Winnipeg), ATP (Calgary) and Western Canada Theatre (Kamloops).  His work has been recognized with 2 Betty Mitchell and 4 Saskatoon and Area Theatre Award nominations for Outstanding Costume Design.\nHe is an  academic with a short attention span but he has a special interest in how Sharon Pollock used scenography and space in her plays.  Currently he is examining the relationship between summer Shakespeare festivals and the public good as well as puttering around with his ongoing interest in technologies, musical theatre, and storytelling.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkNo\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-met