ng cultural norms. Select design credits include: Alice in Wonderland (Guild Festival), Goodnight Bird (Festival Antigonish), C'mon Angie! (Leroy Street), Punk Rock (The Howland Company, Dora Award Nomination), Othello (Driftwood), Of Human Bondage (Magnus), Deceitful Above All Things (Storefront), Hamlet (Hart House). She is a founding member and designer for the Superior Theatre Festival, bringing new and community based performance to Thunder Bay. Nancy also enjoys building the next generation of theatre practitioners through her teaching and design work with Mount Allison University and the University of Windsor. She is the recipient of the Ian and Molly Lindsay Young Design Fellowship, a Tom Patterson Guthrie Award and is a member of the Associated Designers of Canada.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
