oDasha Plett is a transfeminine sound designer and composer. She has worked with the Royal Manitoba Theatre Centre (Tiny Plays, Big Ideas, The Lifespan of a Fact), Theatre Projects Manitoba (Beautiful Man, Goodnight Desdomona (Good Morning Juliet)), Prairie Theatre Exchange (Volare), Sick + Twisted (How It Ends, Trigger Warning), Frances Koncan (Riot Revolt Resist Redux, Hedda Reimagined, Women of the Fur Trade), and Alexandra Elliott (Ellipsis, CONDUCT).\nDasha's independent performance practice has seen work at Cluster Festival, Nuit Blanche, Young Lungs Dance Exchange, WNDX Festival of the Moving Image, and Art Holm. Recent residencies include VideoPool Artists in New Media Residency, PlugIn ICA Summer Institute, 8Days8, and Conversations on Performances at Festival TransAmériques. Dasha is also one half of We Quit Theatre, a performance collective with Gislina Patterson that has toured their work to SummerWorks, OFFTA, Theatre Catapulte, PushOFF, LOMAA, and Buddies in Bad Times. We Quit Theatre’s recent project, Men Explain Things to Us… And We Like It! was commissioned by the Stratford Festival as part of their Viral Transmissions video series.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
