tor whose practice bridges design, fabrication, and fine art. With over two decades of experience in properties, specialty fabrication, and production for theatre and live entertainment, she enjoys collaborating with artists, craftspeople, and storytellers to create engaging and meaningful environments.\nTrained as a sculptor, she brings a strong interest in material exploration, problem-solving and hands-on fabrication to her design practice. Her creative work is driven by an interest in space, movement, and composition, and by how scenic environments influence the way stories are experienced. She enjoys creating spaces that support performers, engage audiences, and contribute to the overall rhythm and visual language of a production.\nLorena holds a B.F.A. in Sculpture from the Pontifical Catholic University of Peru and a M.F.A. in Scenic Design from Penn State University. Her work spans theatre, film, and live entertainment in both Canada and the United States. She is currently Assistant Professor of Scenic and Properties Design at Western Carolina University, while maintaining an active professional practice in both countries.\n \n \nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
