ts in theatre, dance, media arts and music across Canada and internationally. He is a winner of multiple awards and nominations for his work on theatre stages in Canada, including a 2022 Dora Award for Outstanding Achievement in Design (Opera category), and is a 2024 finalist for the Siminovitch Prize, Canada’s largest prize for excellence in the theatre arts.\nSinha’s live sound practice on the concert stage has led to appearances and residencies at MUTEK.JP/MX/MTL, ISEA, NeurIPS, Fiber Festival, Akademie der Künste, EMS Stockholm, Poesiefestival and other venues, and he has released records independently and on Gustaff, Archipel, Other People Records and Establishment. He is a member of the international research group Wilding AI, and currently on faculty at The Creative School, Toronto Metropolitan University.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkNo\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
