er BrookBioJulian Smith is a sound designer, composer, and production artist based in Newfoundland. A graduate of the National Theatre School of Canada’s Production Design and Technical Arts program, Julian has designed and composed for companies including RCAT, Infinitheatre, and the Segal Centre. His work blends original composition, curated music, and innovative soundscapes to heighten storytelling and create immersive theatrical worlds. He has also assisted established designers such as Richard Feren, Brian Kenny, and Troy Slocum. Julian is a member of ADC 659 and was nominated for Best Emerging Artist in Production at the 2024 Montreal English Theatre Awards.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
