uth peoples.\nSelected credits include Hamlet (Honest Fishmongers), Bug (Hardline), Of Mice and Men (Hardline), Selfie (Seizieme), Wilderness (Studio 58), She Mami Wata... (Frank), Dead People's Things (Zee Zee), Never the Last (Delinquent), Oil (Theatre UBC) and S'effondrent les videoclubs (Seizieme).\nWorking with Itsazoo, Jenn has designed for non-traditional venues, including a corporate gladiator fighting ring (The Competition is Fierce), a military tent and a depressing basement suite (Wet) and she worked on her first large scale public event with the 2022 Burnaby Halloween Event Eerie Illusions with Eos Lightmedia.\nIn addition to her design practice, she has worked as a Props Builder, Mask Maker, Wardrobe Coordinator, ASM, Production Manager and Technical Director. \nJenn has worked through out British Columbia, toured nationally and into the United States. She has done multiple seasons with Bard on the Beach and Caravan Farm Theatre in various roles. \nJenn has had the good fortune to have worked as an assistant to Pam Johnson, Drew Facey and Rachel Forbes. \nShe holds a Masters Degree in Design from the University of British Columbia and is a graduate of Studio 58. \nShe has been nominated for several Jessie Richardson awards.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
