InLinkedInBioTristan has more than 15 years experience in lighting and technical design for corporate events and live theatre. He spent 6 seasons as an assistant lighting designer at the Stratford Festival working on 18 different productions. As well as designing at many regional theatres across Canada, Tristan worked as an assistant designer on two shows that transferred to Broadway and a third that toured North America. He is a past recipient of the Wally Russell Lighting Design Internship at the Canadian Opera Company and was the Ian and Molly Lindsay Young Design Fellow at the Stratford Festival. Tristan has lit numerous galas, political events, and awards shows as well as events that have been broadcast nationally. Tristan currently works as Vice President, Production for Bespoke Audio Visual. Highlights include: Canadian Screen Awards 2024, Canada's Walk of Fame Induction Gala 2023, Children's Aid Foundation Teddy Bear Affair 2017-2024, Special Olympics of Canada LIMITLESS Gala, Federal Liberal Election Campaign Fall 2015; Priscilla Queen of the Desert Fall 2010/Winter 2011; Jesus Christ Superstar Spring 2011-Winter 2012; The Wizard of Oz Fall 2012-Winter 2013; 6 Seasons at the Stratford Festival 2010-2015. \nAvailable for Work?NoAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkNo\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
