pectively. She is the lighting designer in residence at the Caravan Farm Theatre, equally at home painting little black boxes with light and shining it into the wild expanse of a woodland night.\nIn 2011 Jill graduated from Capilano University's Technical Theatre program and has since worked with companies such as Touchstone Theatre, Alley Theatre, Rumble Theatre, Pacific Theatre, The Frank Theatre Company, Musical TheatreWorks, Delinquent Theatre, SpeakEasy Theatre, Classic Chic, Kitty Nights Burlesque, and of course, Caravan Farm Theatre. Three of her designs (Bright Blue Future, Never the Last, and Gross Misconduct) have been nominated for Jessie Richardson Theatre Awards.\nAvailable for Work?YesAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkYes\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
