ork created by artists with minority identities, especially those at the intersections of multiple identities. As an emerging disabled designer, she hopes to explore and introduce greater understanding and implementation of disability politics and care-centred practices in theatre spaces. Her most recent credits include Set/Props/Costume Assistant Designer for Perceptual Archaeology (Fire and Rescue), Head of Props for Niizh (Native Earth), Set/Costume Design Assistant for Behind The Moon (Tarragon Theatre), Costume Designer/Head of Props for Between a Wok and a Hot Pot (Cahoots Theatre), and Props Assistant for The First Stone (New Harlem Productions). \nAvailable for Work?NoAvailable for Assistant/Associate WorkNo\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 1000px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-body {\n\t\t\tmax-width: 600px;\n\t\t}\n\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\twidth: 190px;\n\t\theight: 190px;\n\t}\n\t.um-113.um .um-profile-photo a.um-profile-photo-img {\n\t\ttop: -105px;\n\t}\n\t\t\t.um-113.um .um-profile-meta {\n\t\t\tpadding-left: 250px;\n\t\t}\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
